{
  "about": "APICS CPIM-style time-phased MRP scenarios (issue #22, AC1). Weekly buckets: period 1 is the current week (today); on-hand is at the start of period 1. lt and slt (safety lead time) are in periods. lot: L4L, FOQ (foq), POQ (poq periods), MINMAX (reorderMin/reorderMax); min, mult and max are lot-size modifiers applied after the rule, in that order (max splits into equal max lots plus a remainder). gross and sr are gross requirements and scheduled receipts by period; bom lines give quantity per parent. A release in a period below 1 is past due. hand lists the textbook planned orders as [item, qty, releasePeriod, receiptPeriod], derived by hand; prdHand replaces it where a PRD rule (named in prdNote) mandates a different date. handFutures lists, as [item, qty, releasePeriod, receiptPeriod, futuresPeriod], every planned order that is expected later than its receipt: a past-due release is expected in period 1 + lt, and a parent pegged (FIFO) to a late component order is expected at the component's futures period + slt + the parent's lt when that is later; prdHandFutures replaces it for the PRD plan. Orders not listed have no futures date and no delay. reference_mrp.py recomputes both independently and fails if either disagrees with these literals.",
